cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "HybridAuthGuard: Rule-Based Detection and Triage of Authentication Attacks"
authors:
  - family-names: "Deegbe"
    given-names: "Cephas Dotse Klenam"
date-released: "2026-10-17"
version: "3.0.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/klenam0/HybridAuthGuard"
license: MIT
type: software
keywords:
  - intrusion-detection
  - anomaly-detection
  - isolation-forest
  - rule-based-detection
  - mitre-attack
  - risk-based-authentication
abstract: >
  A multi-agent pipeline that detects and triages authentication attacks in a
  stream of login events, evaluated on the RBA Dataset. The default
  configuration uses eight windowed rule detectors, label-free incident triage
  and capped simulated response tiers, with alerts mapped to MITRE ATT&CK and
  optional explanations from a local LLM; it has no machine-learning detection
  step. A legacy mode keeps the original rules and the Isolation Forest model,
  whose training rows were filtered using the attack labels. Developed as a
  final-year BSc Information Technology research project at the University of
  Ghana.
